            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for I could not hear it, then the Hindi for please write it down."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: सही",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सही (sahī) — \"right, correct\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सही (sahī) दाम — \"the right price\". Said alone, सही (sahī)! agrees: \"right!\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सही (sahī) is a loan from Arabic ṣaḥīḥ, \"sound, correct\", which reached Hindi through Persian. Its Arabic root is ṣ-ḥ-ḥ (Lane)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A word for getting it right."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
